findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase addressed the from_file_or_default swallowing all errors. TEA
    tests mention config loading but no test specifically checks that parse/permission
    errors are distinguished from NotFound. Dev implemented from_file but no evidence
    of error discrimination. Reviewer did not flag this specific issue.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: 'Dev implemented sanitized Display for ServerError and ConfigError variants.
    Reviewer verified: ''Display sanitizes ServerError and ConfigError internals.''
    TEA also had security tests for CWE-209. However, Reviewer flagged NotFound still
    leaks resource identifiers, so partial catch. The core issue of eprintln leaking
    via Display was partially addressed.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged: '--tenant accepts raw String, not validated TenantId\
    \ \u2014 cli.rs:37' and recommended validating tenant input as TenantId at the\
    \ CLI boundary. TEA also had CRLF rejection tests but did not require TenantId\
    \ type usage specifically."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that 6 dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. Reviewer verified 'Workspace dependencies properly declared
    at root level' but missed the specific deps using direct versions.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged: 'RawConfig silently ignores unknown TOML fields \u2014\
    \ config.rs:16-22' and recommended #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]. This directly\
    \ addresses the concern about token field being silently ignored."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...) in the test suite. TEA wrote config tests but the specific vacuous assertion
    was not flagged by any phase.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the test with zero assertions that only checks non-panic
    via 'let _ = config'. TEA wrote config tests but did not flag this pattern.
